  "schematicNotes": [
    {
      "id": "n_cavity_notes",
      "text": "BULKHEAD BH-A NOTES\nBH-A pin 83: EHPS pump enable, +12 V from the LOGIC MRS 7.5 A fuse (fed by the EPS enable relay pin 87, ignition-switched). Moved from bulkhead B 2026-09-28 because the pump ECU signal (A27) is on connector A. The wire to the pump (plug C pin 1) is drawn on ST185-EngineRoom-C.\nBH-A pin 84: ECU A27 (Aux 7) speed pulse to the EHPS pump plug B pin 2, drawn on ST185-EngineRoom-C.\nBH-A pin 85: EHPS pump plug B pin 5 switches the EPS relay coil pin 85 (glove box) to ground (DECISIONS R22).",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 510,
        "y": 180
      },
      "width": 390
    },
    {
      "id": "n_sp_gndout_fit",
      "text": "sp_gndout_eng SPLICE FIT: four 20 AWG wires = one 14 AWG combined (Wire Barn Combined Wire Gauge Calculator, https://www.wirebarn.com/Combined-Wire-Gauge-Calculator_ep_42.html), inside the GENERIC CRIMP SPLICE 14-10 range. Splices are sized by combined gauge (Daniel 2026-09-28). harness.design's per-wire 'wires are too thin' warning on this splice is a known false alarm.",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 390,
        "y": 480
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n_drb102",
      "width": 390,
      "color": "Orange",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 390,
        "y": -120
      },
      "text": "BULKHEAD = ONE DRB102 CONNECTOR (Daniel 2026-10-12, shared-connector rule). bh_a_eng is the whole 102-cavity plug with TE's cavity numbers. A and B are only our names for its sections. Cavities marked N/C here are wired on ST185-ECU-engine - see ST185-ECU-engine (DRB 3-8, 43, 48-49, 54-55, 60, 62-102); their contacts and sealing plugs are counted there."
    },
    {
      "id": "n_cavity_notes_b",
      "text": "GEARBOX SPEED SENSOR NOTE\nGearbox VSS (Toyota 83181-20040), pin 3 speed output to BH-B pin 68, then ECU B29 (DI 8). Actual road speed. 12 V direct, no divider - the Link DI is +/-50 V tolerant with a selectable 4k7 pull-up to 12 V. PCLink DI 8 pull-up ON (sot/channels.csv B29).",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1860,
        "y": 4380
      },
      "width": 390
    },
    {
      "id": "n_drb102_b",
      "width": 390,
      "color": "Orange",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 330,
        "y": 4740
      },
      "text": "BULKHEAD = ONE DRB102 CONNECTOR (Daniel 2026-10-12, shared-connector rule). bh_b_eng is the whole 102-cavity plug with TE's cavity numbers. A and B are only our names for its sections. Cavities marked N/C here are wired on ST185-ECU-engine - see ST185-ECU-engine (DRB 1-2, 9-42, 44-47, 50-53, 56-59, 61); their contacts and sealing plugs are counted there."
    }
  ],
